      "text_raw": "The output spectrum for the\nmaximum input signal is\nshown in this slide.\nThe noise floor at low fre-\nquencies is quite low. The\nintegrated noise is shown as\nwell. For an input signal of\n1 kHz, the SNR is about\n76 dB.\nDistortion is already\nclearly visible, however.\nSecond-order distortion is\npresent because of the\nsingle-ended input drive\nused for this measurement.\nThe SNDR (signal to noise\nand distortion ratio) is then only about 62 dB.\nThe bandwidth is about 16 kHz, corresponding to an OSR of 48.",
      "text": "The output spectrum for the maximum input signal is shown in this slide. The noise floor at low frequencies is quite low. The integrated noise is shown as well. For an input signal of 1 kHz, the SNR is about 76 dB. Distortion is already clearly visible, however. Second-order distortion is present because of the single-ended input drive used for this measurement. The SNDR (signal to noise and distortion ratio) is then only about 62 dB. The bandwidth is about 16 kHz, corresponding to an OSR of 48."
    }
